# How to cite this software. Read by GitHub (the "Cite this repository" button) and by
# Zenodo, so a reader does not have to guess at a citation and get it wrong.
#
# This file exists because a prior review named its absence as a reviewer's first
# question: "How do I cite this software, and who are the authors with their ORCIDs and
# affiliations?" It had no answer anywhere in the project.
#
# BOTH ORCIDs ARE RECORDED, supplied by the authors on 2026-09-04. The entity author has
# none and never will: an ORCID identifies a PERSON.
#
# They were held empty until the strings themselves were in hand, on the reasoning that an
# invented or guessed ORCID is worse than a missing one — it resolves to a REAL PERSON who is
# not the author, and a citation is exactly the place that error propagates. A test still
# forbids shipping the all-zeros placeholder, and it is NOT SPELLED OUT ANYWHERE IN THIS FILE
# on purpose: the guard matches the literal string, so writing it here — even inside a comment
# explaining the guard — trips it. That has now happened twice, to two different people
# describing the same rule, which is the guard working and the reason this paragraph is
# phrased the long way round.
#
# EACH CHECK DIGIT WAS VERIFIED before it was written here, not merely pasted. An ORCID
# carries an ISO 7064 MOD 11-2 checksum over its first fifteen digits, so a transposed pair
# is detectable rather than silent — and a silently wrong ORCID is precisely the failure the
# paragraph above refuses. Both computed to the digit they carry.
#
# AUTHOR ORDER IS THE AUTHORS' TO SET and is recorded here as decided on 2026-09-01: Taylor
# Thompson first as the author of the software, Christophe Rodriguez second as thesis
# director, and Plateforme GenoBioMICS third as an entity — see the note beside it.
# JOSS applies authorship criteria based on contribution to the SOFTWARE — worth re-reading
# before submission, since the reviewers ask.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: runprov
abstract: >-
  Records what a script read, wrote and ran as, in a form a checker can verify. Inputs are
  hashed at the moment they are opened, the resulting pin is written into the artifact
  itself rather than only into a sidecar, and the pin is deterministic so that a changed
  header means changed inputs. Zero runtime dependencies.
version: 0.1.0
# NO `date-released` YET, and that is a statement rather than an omission: this version has
# not been released. Zenodo and GitHub render a citation without a year until it is set, and
# a citation without a year is a poor one -- so `python ci.py release-check` (which `build`
# runs, and which ships beside this file) refuses a release whose CHANGELOG says released
# while this field is missing, and refuses a version TAG whose CHANGELOG section still reads
# `[Unreleased]`. Set it to the tag date, YYYY-MM-DD. Inventing a date for an unreleased
# package would be the same class of error as the placeholder ORCID this file already
# refuses.
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/Taylor-Nicole/runprov"
keywords:
  - provenance
  - reproducibility
  - research software
  - data lineage
authors:
  - family-names: Thompson
    given-names: Taylor
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-0091-0319"
    affiliation: "Plateforme GenoBioMICS, Hôpital Henri-Mondor, AP-HP · INSERM Unité U955, équipe Pawlotsky · Créteil, France"
  - family-names: Rodriguez
    given-names: Christophe
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9817-5006"
    affiliation: "Plateforme GenoBioMICS, Hôpital Henri-Mondor, AP-HP · INSERM Unité U955, équipe Pawlotsky · Créteil, France"
  # AN ENTITY AUTHOR, which CFF supports alongside people — a `name` instead of
  # `family-names`/`given-names`. This is how the platform gets credited in a citation
  # WITHOUT appearing in the copyright line, which names who holds the economic rights and is
  # a different question. The full institutional form is in `name` because a citation
  # renderer shows only that field: "Plateforme GenoBioMICS" alone would reach a reader with
  # no idea whose it is.
  - name: "Plateforme GenoBioMICS, Hôpital Henri-Mondor, AP-HP"
    city: Créteil
    country: FR
